---
import trustpointLogo from "../img/trustpoint_labs_logo.svg?url";
import trustpointFavicon from "../img/trustpoint_favicon.png?url";

import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/400.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/500.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/600.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/700.css";

import "../styles/global.css";

const githubUrl = "https://github.com/Trustpoint-Project";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <title>Industrial PKI Engineering & Integration | Trustpoint Labs</title>

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Vendor-independent industrial PKI engineering, integration and security consulting. Automate machine certificates, connect OT systems and develop custom solutions."
    />

    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />

    <link
      rel="canonical"
      href="https://trustpoint-labs.com/engineering-integration/"
    />

    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Trustpoint Labs" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Industrial PKI Engineering & Integration | Trustpoint Labs" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Vendor-independent industrial PKI integration, machine identity engineering, custom automation and security consulting for OT environments." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://trustpoint-labs.com/engineering-integration/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://trustpoint-labs.com/og-image.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Trustpoint Labs — Industrial PKI Engineering & Integration" />

    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href={trustpointFavicon}
    />
  </head>

  <body>

    <header class="shell">
      <a
        class="logo-link"
        href="/"
        aria-label="Trustpoint Labs"
      >
        <img
          class="logo"
          src={trustpointLogo}
          alt="Trustpoint Labs"
          width="205"
          height="115"
        />
      </a>

      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="/">Home</a>

        <a
          class="github"
          href={githubUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          GitHub
          <span>↗︎</span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="engineering-page">

      <section class="engineering-hero shell" id="overview">
        <div class="section-label">
          <span class="square"></span>
          ENGINEERING & INTEGRATION
        </div>

        <div class="engineering-hero-grid">
          <div>
            <h1>
              Industrial PKI Engineering &amp; Integration.
            </h1>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="engineering-lede">
              Industrial devices and OT systems often rely on fragmented certificate
              processes, incompatible interfaces and complex trust architectures.
              Trustpoint Labs helps you design, integrate and automate machine identity
              and certificate lifecycle management using open standards and
              technologies suited to your environment.
            </p>

            <p class="engineering-note">
              We work vendor-independently with existing PKI platforms, devices
              and applications. Our open-source Trustpoint platform is one option
              for bringing certificate lifecycle management closer to industrial systems.
              <a class="engineering-inline-link" href="https://github.com/Trustpoint-Project/trustpoint" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the open-source project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="engineering-layout shell">

        <aside class="engineering-sidebar" aria-label="Engineering page navigation">
          <nav>
            <a href="#overview" class="engineering-sidebar-link is-active">Overview</a>
            <a href="#project-journey" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Project Journey</a>
            <a href="#integration" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Integration</a>
            <a href="#consulting" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Security Consulting</a>
            <a href="#custom-engineering" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Custom Engineering</a>
            <a href="#example-projects" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Integration Scenarios</a>
            <a href="#deliverables" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Deliverables</a>
            <a href="#engineering-vs-support" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Engineering vs. Support</a>
            <a href="#start-project" class="engineering-sidebar-link">Start a Project</a>
          </nav>
        </aside>

        <div class="engineering-content">

          <section id="project-journey" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              PROJECT JOURNEY
            </div>

            <h2>From PKI assessment to operational handover.</h2>
            <p>Whether you need to connect an existing certificate authority to industrial devices, automate renewal, or establish machine identities for a new product, we structure the work around your technical constraints and agreed outcomes.</p>

            <div class="journey-list">
              <article class="journey-item">
                <span class="journey-index">01</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Assess & Design</h3>
                  <p>
                    We assess devices, applications, existing PKI, trust boundaries,
                    network restrictions and security requirements. Where relevant,
                    we consider applicable standards and regulatory requirements
                    when designing the integration.
                  </p>

                  <h4>Typical deliverables</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Target architecture</li>
                    <li>Integration scope</li>
                    <li>Protocol and interface requirements</li>
                    <li>Implementation plan and agreed responsibilities</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article class="journey-item">
                <span class="journey-index">02</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Integrate & Implement</h3>
                  <p>
                    We configure Trustpoint, integrate connected PKI systems,
                    implement enrollment and lifecycle workflows and develop
                    custom connectors or automation where necessary. Delivery can
                    be independent or in collaboration with customer teams.
                  </p>

                  <h4>Typical deliverables</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Configured Trustpoint environment</li>
                    <li>Implemented integrations</li>
                    <li>Working enrollment and lifecycle workflows</li>
                    <li>Customer-specific extensions where required</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article class="journey-item">
                <span class="journey-index">03</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Validate & Deploy</h3>
                  <p>
                    We validate the integration against project-specific acceptance
                    criteria, including functional behavior, device interoperability
                    and certificate lifecycle workflows, and prepare the deployment
                    for the agreed operational environment. Extensive security
                    assessments, penetration tests and formal conformity assessments
                    require separate agreement.
                  </p>

                  <h4>Typical deliverables</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Validation results</li>
                    <li>Production configuration</li>
                    <li>Deployment checklist</li>
                    <li>Implementation documentation</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article class="journey-item">
                <span class="journey-index">04</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Handover & Operate</h3>
                  <p>
                    We document the implementation, provide operational guidance
                    and conduct a project-specific handover. The customer or their
                    designated provider remains responsible for operations. Optional
                    support and SLA agreements, as well as additional workshops or
                    training, are available separately.
                  </p>

                  <h4>Typical deliverables</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Technical documentation</li>
                    <li>Handover session</li>
                    <li>Operational guidance</li>
                    <li>Optional transition to Trustpoint Labs Support</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="integration" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              INTEGRATION
            </div>

            <h2>Integrate industrial devices with your existing PKI.</h2>

            <p>
              Industrial certificate automation must work across different devices,
              vendors, certificate authorities and operational networks. We take a
              vendor-independent, open-standards-first approach to connecting IT and
              OT infrastructure. Where appropriate, Trustpoint can serve as a local
              certificate lifecycle layer or integrate with an existing PKI. The
              actual architecture depends on device capabilities, network segmentation
              and connectivity requirements.
              <a class="engineering-inline-link" href="/use-cases/">Explore our application areas <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            </p>

            <div class="capability-grid">
              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>Enrollment protocols</h3>
                <p>CMP and EST integration for automated certificate enrollment and lifecycle workflows.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>REST & API integration</h3>
                <p>Connect applications and automation workflows to Trustpoint through supported APIs.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>OPC UA / GDS</h3>
                <p>Integrate Trustpoint into OPC UA certificate-management and GDS-based environments.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>Enterprise PKI & RA integration</h3>
                <p>Integrate Trustpoint with external CAs, RAs and certificate management platforms, including relevant architecture, configuration and interface workflows.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>Device onboarding</h3>
                <p>Implement secure onboarding and certificate lifecycle workflows for connected devices across our application areas.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>Legacy & restricted environments</h3>
                <p>Integrate legacy devices and systems in segmented, restricted-connectivity or air-gapped environments, including cases without modern enrollment interfaces.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="consulting" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              INDUSTRIAL SECURITY CONSULTING
            </div>
            <h2>Plan machine identities and trust before deployment.</h2>
            <p>
              Industrial operators and equipment manufacturers need certificate policies,
              device onboarding strategies and trust models that fit long-lived OT assets.
              We help assess the current situation, identify integration constraints and
              develop a practical industrial PKI architecture without requiring a specific
              PKI vendor or deployment platform.
            </p>
            <div class="capability-grid">
              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>PKI architecture &amp; trust models</h3>
                <p>Define certificate authorities, registration flows, trust boundaries and lifecycle responsibilities across devices, machines and operators.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="capability-card">
                <h3>Standards &amp; security requirements</h3>
                <p>Assess relevant technical requirements and integration options for certificate-based security, including IEC 62443-related architecture considerations where applicable. Formal compliance assessment is separately scoped.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
            <p>
              Consulting can be delivered as an independent assessment or as the first
              phase of an engineering project. <a class="engineering-inline-link" href="/#contact">Discuss an industrial PKI assessment <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="custom-engineering" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              CUSTOM ENGINEERING
            </div>

            <h2>Build custom PKI integrations where standards are not enough.</h2>

            <p>
              Legacy devices, proprietary interfaces and specialized operational workflows
              do not always fit standard certificate enrollment mechanisms. We develop
              customer-specific connectors, device integrations and automation for the
              agreed PKI architecture. Where Trustpoint is used, reusable improvements
              can be contributed to the open-source project; proprietary extensions
              can remain separate, subject to agreed licensing and ownership terms.
            </p>

            <ul class="engineering-list">
              <li>Custom connectors and plugins</li>
              <li>Customer-specific APIs</li>
              <li>Device-specific onboarding logic</li>
              <li>Web-UI Automation profiles</li>
              <li>Proprietary device interfaces</li>
              <li>Customer-specific workflows</li>
              <li>Custom deployment automation</li>
              <li>Trustpoint extensions required for the deployment</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Custom extensions are validated against the agreed scope and
              acceptance criteria. Ongoing maintenance and compatibility updates
              can be arranged separately. Embedding Trustpoint into your own
              product or brand? See our <a href="/oem/">OEM &amp; White-Label services</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="example-projects" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              INTEGRATION SCENARIOS
            </div>

            <h2>Industrial PKI integration scenarios.</h2>
            <p>Examples of problems we can address using Trustpoint or other suitable PKI technologies. These are illustrative applications, not customer project references.</p>

            <div class="project-grid">
              <article class="project-card">
                <span>01</span>
                <h3>Enterprise PKI Integration</h3>
                <p>
                  Connect industrial certificate workflows with existing enterprise CAs,
                  registration processes and lifecycle policies, using Trustpoint where suitable.
                </p>
              </article>

              <article class="project-card">
                <span>02</span>
                <h3>Industrial Device Enrollment</h3>
                <p>
                  Replace manual certificate provisioning with enrollment and renewal
                  workflows using EST, CMP or device-supported alternatives.
                </p>
              </article>

              <article class="project-card">
                <span>03</span>
                <h3>OPC UA Certificate Management</h3>
                <p>
                  Reduce manual certificate handling by integrating compatible OPC UA
                  applications with GDS-based certificate-management workflows.
                </p>
              </article>

              <article class="project-card">
                <span>04</span>
                <h3>Brownfield Device Integration</h3>
                <p>
                  Address legacy devices lacking standard enrollment interfaces with
                  validated device-specific workflows, including Web-UI Automation where supported.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
            <p>
              Explore the detailed deployment patterns and prerequisites on our
              <a class="engineering-inline-link" href="/use-cases/">Industrial PKI Use Cases page <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="deliverables" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              DELIVERABLES
            </div>

            <h2>What an engagement can produce.</h2>

            <p>
              Every engagement includes technical documentation and handover
              appropriate to its scope. Specific artifacts and acceptance criteria
              are agreed for each assignment; source code and development assets
              are handed over as contractually agreed.
            </p>

            <ul class="engineering-list two-column-list">
              <li>Integration architecture</li>
              <li>Configured Trustpoint deployment</li>
              <li>Implemented interfaces and workflows</li>
              <li>Custom connectors or automation</li>
              <li>Functional and interoperability validation results</li>
              <li>Deployment documentation</li>
              <li>Operational documentation</li>
              <li>Technical handover</li>
              <li>Optional transition into commercial support</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="engineering-vs-support" class="engineering-section">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              ENGINEERING VS. SUPPORT
            </div>

            <h2>Build and change vs. restore and troubleshoot.</h2>

            <div class="compare-grid">
              <article class="compare-card">
                <h3>Engineering & Integration</h3>
                <p>
                  Designs and integrates industrial PKI architectures, automates machine identities and develops custom solutions using Trustpoint or other suitable technology.
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li>New integrations</li>
                  <li>Deployment projects</li>
                  <li>Device onboarding</li>
                  <li>Custom automation</li>
                  <li>Custom development</li>
                  <li>Architecture work</li>
                </ul>
              </article>

              <article class="compare-card">
                <h3>Commercial Support</h3>
                <p>
                  Provides agreed technical assistance, troubleshooting and
                  incident resolution under optional support or SLA contracts.
                  The customer or designated operator retains operational responsibility;
                  managed operations are not currently offered.
                </p>
                <a class="engineering-inline-link" href="/support/">
                  Learn about commercial support
                  <span aria-hidden="true">→︎</span>
                </a>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="start-project" class="engineering-section engineering-cta">
            <div class="section-label compact-label">
              <span class="square"></span>
              START A PROJECT
            </div>

            <h2>Let's discuss your project.</h2>

            <p>
              Tell us which certificates, devices or PKI integration problems you need
              to solve. Start with a free, non-binding initial conversation about your
              environment, technical objectives and integration requirements.
              We support focused engineering tasks on a time-and-material basis
              as well as scoped projects with defined milestones and deliverables.
              Detailed assessments, consulting and workshops can be agreed separately.
            </p>

            <a class="button button-primary" href="/#contact">
              Discuss your project
              <span>→︎</span>
            </a>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>

    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="footer-inner shell">
        <a href="/" aria-label="Trustpoint Labs">
          <img
            class="footer-logo"
            src={trustpointLogo}
            alt="Trustpoint Labs"
            width="180"
            height="101"
          />
        </a>

        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <a href="/support/">Support</a>
        <a href="/use-cases/">Use Cases</a>
          <a href="/imprint">Imprint</a>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      const links = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.engineering-sidebar-link'));
      const sections = links
        .map((link) => document.querySelector(link.getAttribute('href')))
        .filter(Boolean);

      const setActive = (id) => {
        links.forEach((link) => {
          link.classList.toggle('is-active', link.getAttribute('href') === `#${id}`);
        });
      };

      const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => {
          const visible = entries
            .filter((entry) => entry.isIntersecting)
            .sort((a, b) => b.intersectionRatio - a.intersectionRatio);

          if (visible.length > 0) {
            setActive(visible[0].target.id);
          }
        },
        {
          rootMargin: '-18% 0px -65% 0px',
          threshold: [0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75]
        }
      );

      sections.forEach((section) => observer.observe(section));
    </script>

    <style>
      .engineering-page {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .engineering-hero {
        padding-block: 86px 92px;
      }

      .engineering-hero-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 0.85fr);
        gap: clamp(56px, 8vw, 120px);
        align-items: end;
      }

      .engineering-hero h1 {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: 900px;
        font-size: clamp(52px, 6.4vw, 92px);
        line-height: 0.98;
        letter-spacing: -0.045em;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .engineering-lede {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--black);
        font-size: 21px;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .engineering-note {
        margin: 28px 0 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .engineering-layout {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 250px minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: clamp(48px, 7vw, 104px);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .engineering-sidebar {
        position: relative;
        padding-top: 58px;
      }

      .engineering-sidebar nav {
        position: sticky;
        top: 28px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: stretch;
        gap: 0;
      }

      .engineering-sidebar-link {
        display: block;
        padding: 11px 0 11px 16px;
        border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.35;
      }

      .engineering-sidebar-link:hover,
      .engineering-sidebar-link:focus-visible,
      .engineering-sidebar-link.is-active {
        color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
        border-left-color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
      }

      .engineering-sidebar-link.is-active {
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .engineering-content {
        min-width: 0;
      }

      .engineering-section {
        padding-block: 88px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
        scroll-margin-top: 36px;
      }

      .compact-label {
        margin-bottom: 26px;
      }

      .engineering-section h2 {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(38px, 4.7vw, 62px);
        line-height: 1.02;
      }

      .engineering-section > p {
        max-width: 820px;
        margin: 26px 0 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 18px;
        line-height: 1.65;
      }

      .journey-list {
        margin-top: 52px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--black);
      }

      .journey-item {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 72px minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 28px;
        padding: 34px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .journey-index {
        color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .journey-item h3,
      .capability-card h3,
      .project-card h3,
      .compare-card h3 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 24px;
        line-height: 1.2;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      }

      .journey-item p,
      .capability-card p,
      .project-card p,
      .compare-card p {
        margin: 12px 0 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .journey-item h4 {
        margin: 22px 0 0;
        font-size: 14px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }

      .journey-item ul,
      .compare-card ul {
        margin: 12px 0 0;
        padding-left: 18px;
      }

      .journey-item li,
      .compare-card li {
        margin: 5px 0;
      }

      .capability-grid,
      .project-grid,
      .compare-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 18px;
        margin-top: 48px;
      }

      .capability-card,
      .project-card,
      .compare-card {
        min-height: 220px;
        padding: 28px;
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-top: 3px solid var(--trustpoint-blue);
        background: #fff;
      }

      .project-card > span {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 28px;
        color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .engineering-list {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 0 32px;
        margin: 42px 0 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .engineering-list li {
        position: relative;
        padding: 16px 0 16px 24px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .engineering-list li::before {
        content: "→︎";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
      }

      .two-column-list {
        max-width: 980px;
      }

      .engineering-inline-link {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 10px;
        margin-top: 28px;
        color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
        font-size: 14px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .engineering-inline-link:hover,
      .engineering-inline-link:focus-visible {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      .engineering-cta {
        border-bottom: 0;
      }

      .engineering-cta .button {
        margin-top: 34px;
      }

      @media (max-width: 920px) {
        .engineering-hero-grid,
        .engineering-layout {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .engineering-sidebar {
          padding-top: 0;
          border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
          border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
        }

        .engineering-sidebar nav {
          position: static;
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: row;
          overflow-x: auto;
          gap: 18px;
          padding: 14px 0;
        }

        .engineering-sidebar-link {
          flex: 0 0 auto;
          padding: 0;
          border-left: 0;
          border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
        }

        .engineering-sidebar-link.is-active {
          border-bottom-color: var(--trustpoint-blue);
        }

        .capability-grid,
        .project-grid,
        .compare-grid,
        .engineering-list {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .engineering-hero {
          padding-block: 58px 64px;
        }

        .engineering-section {
          padding-block: 64px;
        }

        .journey-item {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          gap: 12px;
        }
      }
    </style>

  </body>
</html>
